<title>USA: Sears to buy Florida pest control business.</title>
<headline>Sears to buy Florida pest control business.</headline>
<dateline>HOFFMAN ESTATES, Ill. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co said Monday it had agreed to acquire  All America Termite and Pest Control Inc, a pest control business in Florida that posted 1996 revenues of more than $100 million.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed. The deal is expected to close in March, Sears said.</p>
<p>All America has been operating as a licensee of Sears since 1982 as part of the Sears Home Services division, Sears said.</p>
<p>Sears shares were off 1/2 at 49-1/4 in afternoon trading.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
